Solution:

1. Install the JWT Editor extension from the Burp BApp Store.
2. Log in using:
   wiener:peter
3. In Burp → Proxy → HTTP history, find the:
   GET /my-account
   request.
4. Send the request to Burp Repeater.
5. Change the path to:
   GET /admin
6. Open the following endpoint in the browser:
   /jwks.json
7. Copy the JWK object from inside the keys array.
8. In Burp, go to JWT Editor Keys.
9. Click New RSA Key.
10. Make sure JWK is selected, paste the copied JWK, then click OK.
11. Right-click the generated key and select Copy Public Key as PEM.
12. Open the Decoder tab and Base64-encode the copied PEM key.
13. Copy the resulting Base64 value.
14. Return to JWT Editor Keys and click New Symmetric Key.
15. Click Generate.
16. Replace the value of the k property with the Base64-encoded PEM:
    "k": "<BASE64-ENCODED-PEM>"
17. Save the key.
18. Return to the GET /admin request in Burp Repeater.
19. Open the JSON Web Token tab.
20. Change the alg value in the JWT header to:
    "alg": "HS256"
21. Change the sub claim to:
    "sub": "administrator"
22. Click Sign.
23. Select the symmetric key generated earlier.
24. Make sure Don't modify header is selected, then click OK.
25. Send the request:
    GET /admin
26. Find the delete endpoint in the response:
    /admin/delete?username=carlos
27. Send a request to:
    GET /admin/delete?username=carlos
28. The lab is solved.
